### Readonly classes — version introduced, restrictions, and inheritance rule

Source: https://github.com/php/doc-en/blob/master/language/oop5/basic.xml

A readonly class (PHP 8.2.0+) cannot use #[AllowDynamicProperties], cannot have untyped properties, cannot have static properties, and can only be extended by another readonly class.

```php
<?php
#[
AllowDynamicProperties]
readonly class Foo {
}

// Fatal error: Cannot apply #[AllowDynamicProperties] to readonly class Foo
?>

<?php
readonly class Foo
{
    public $bar;
}

// Fatal error: Readonly property Foo::$bar must have type
?>

<?php
readonly class Foo
{
    public static int $bar;
}

// Fatal error: Readonly class Foo cannot declare static properties
?>
```

--------------------------------

### Readonly properties — version introduced, initialization, and immutability

Source: https://github.com/php/doc-en/blob/master/language/oop5/properties.xml

Declares a readonly property (PHP 8.1.0+), initializes it in the constructor, demonstrates legal read, and shows that reassignment throws an Error.

```php
<?php

class Test {
   public readonly string $prop;

   public function __construct(string $prop) {
       // Legal initialization.
       $this->prop = $prop;
   }
}

$test = new Test("foobar");
// Legal read.
var_dump($test->prop); // string(6) "foobar"

// Illegal reassignment. It does not matter that the assigned value is the same.
$test->prop = "foobar";
// Error: Cannot modify readonly property Test::$prop
?>
```

--------------------------------

### Inheritance — override restriction between read-write and readonly

Source: https://github.com/php/doc-en/blob/master/language/oop5/inheritance.xml

It is not allowed to override a read-write property with a readonly property or vice versa.

```php
<?php

class A {
    public int $prop;
}
class B extends A {
    // Illegal: read-write -> readonly
    public readonly int $prop;
}
?>
```

