### Fixing parameterByRef.type via @param-out

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/errors/parameterByRef.type.md

Uses the @param-out PHPDoc tag to explicitly declare the output type of the by-reference parameter.

```diff-php
 class Foo
 {
+	/** @param-out int $p */
 	public function doFoo(string &$p): void
 	{
 		$p = 1;
 	}
```

--------------------------------

### Fix: Replace @pure-unless-callable-is-impure with @phpstan-pure

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/errors/pureFunction.redundantUnlessCallable.md

To fix the redundancy, replace the `@pure-unless-callable-is-impure` tag with `@phpstan-pure` when the callable parameter is already guaranteed to be pure.

```php
<?php declare(strict_types = 1);

/**
 * @param pure-callable(int): int $f
 * @param array<int> $arr
 * @return array<int>
 * @phpstan-pure
 */
function myMap(callable $f, array $arr): array
{
	$result = [];
	foreach ($arr as $i => $v) {
		$result[$i] = $f($v);
	}

	return $result;
}
```

--------------------------------

### Fix: Narrow by-ref type with @param-out

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan/blob/2.2.x/website/errors/parameterByRef.tooWideBool.md

To fix the 'too wide bool' issue, narrow the by-reference parameter's type using a `@param-out` PHPDoc tag if it's always set to a specific boolean value.

```php
