### UnusedMethodCollector Implementation

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/03-rules.md

Implements the Collector interface to identify and collect private methods within a class. It listens for `ClassMethod` nodes and returns an array containing details of private methods, including their class, name, file, and line number. This collector is intended to be processed by a `CollectedDataNode` rule.

```php
use PHPStan\Collectors\Collector;
use PHPStan\Collectors\CollectedData;
use PHPStan\Analyser\Scope;
use PhpParser\Node;
use PhpParser\Node\Stmt\ClassMethod;

final class UnusedMethodCollector implements Collector {
    public function getNodeType(): string {
        return ClassMethod::class;
    }

    public function processNode(Node $node, Scope $scope): CollectorData {
        // Collect all private methods
        if (!$node->isPrivate()) {
            return [];
        }

        $class = $scope->getClassReflection();
        if ($class === null) {
            return [];
        }

        return [
            'unused_methods' => [
                [
                    'class' => $class->getName(),
                    'method' => $node->name->toString(),
                    'file' => $scope->getFile(),
                    'line' => $node->getStartLine(),
                ]
            ]
        ];
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### UnusedMethodRule Processing Collected Data

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/03-rules.md

Implements the `Rule` interface to process data aggregated by collectors. This rule listens for `CollectedDataNode` and accesses the collected data to identify unused methods. It serves as an example of how to consume data gathered by a collector like `UnusedMethodCollector`.

```php
use PHPStan\Rules\Rule;
use PHPStan\Node\CollectedDataNode;
use PhpParser\Node;

final class UnusedMethodRule implements Rule {
    public function getNodeType(): string {
        return CollectedDataNode::class;
    }

    public function processNode(Node $node, Scope $scope): array {
        // $node->getData() contains aggregated collector results
        $data = $node->getData();
        $unusedMethods = $data['unused_methods'] ?? [];

        // Check which methods are actually used...
        // Report unused ones

        return [];
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Create a Custom Rule

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/09-api-quick-reference.md

Implement the Rule interface to define custom rules. Specify the node type to listen for and implement the processNode method to analyze the node and return errors.

```php
use PHPStan\Rules\Rule;
use PHPStan\Rules\RuleErrorBuilder;
use PHPStan\Analyser\Scope;
use PhpParser\Node;
use PhpParser\Node\Expr\FuncCall;

final class MyRule implements Rule {
    public function getNodeType(): string {
        return FuncCall::class; // Listen for function calls
    }

    public function processNode(Node $node, Scope $scope): array {
        // $node is a FuncCall
        $functionName = $node->name;

        if ($functionName instanceof Node\Name) {
            $name = $scope->resolveName($functionName);

            if ($name === 'dangerous_function') {
                return [
                    RuleErrorBuilder::message('Forbidden function')
                        ->identifier('app.rules.forbiddenFunction')
                        ->line($node->getStartLine())
                        ->build(),
                ];
            }
        }

        return [];
    }
}
```

--------------------------------

### Use RuleErrorBuilder for Custom Rule Errors

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/UPGRADING.md

Custom rules must now use RuleErrorBuilder to report errors, providing an identifier for each error. This replaces the older method of returning plain strings.

```php
return ['My error'];
```

```php
return [
    RuleErrorBuilder::message('My error')
        ->identifier('my.error')
        ->build(),
];
```

--------------------------------

### Accessing PHPDoc Tags from a Method Reflection

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/05-phpdoc.md

This snippet shows how to retrieve PHPDoc tags like @param and @return from a method's reflection. It specifically handles cases where the reflection originates from a PhpMethodFromParserNodeReflection.

```php
// In a rule or extension
$method = $classRef->getMethod('myMethod', $scope);

// Get PHPDoc tags
$methodRefOrig = $method->getNativeReflection();
if ($methodRefOrig instanceof PhpMethodFromParserNodeReflection) {
    $phpDocBlock = $methodRefOrig->getResolvedPhpDocBlock();

    foreach ($phpDocBlock->getParamTags() as $paramTag) {
        $paramType = $paramTag->getType();
        echo $paramTag->getParameter()->getName();
    }

    $returnTag = $phpDocBlock->getReturnTag();
    if ($returnTag !== null) {
        echo $returnTag->getType()->describe(...);
    }
}
```

