### Accessing PHPDoc Tags from a Method Reflection

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/05-phpdoc.md

This snippet shows how to retrieve PHPDoc tags like @param and @return from a method's reflection. It specifically handles cases where the reflection originates from a PhpMethodFromParserNodeReflection.

```php
// In a rule or extension
$method = $classRef->getMethod('myMethod', $scope);

// Get PHPDoc tags
$methodRefOrig = $method->getNativeReflection();
if ($methodRefOrig instanceof PhpMethodFromParserNodeReflection) {
    $phpDocBlock = $methodRefOrig->getResolvedPhpDocBlock();

    foreach ($phpDocBlock->getParamTags() as $paramTag) {
        $paramType = $paramTag->getType();
        echo $paramTag->getParameter()->getName();
    }

    $returnTag = $phpDocBlock->getReturnTag();
    if ($returnTag !== null) {
        echo $returnTag->getType()->describe(...);
    }
}
```

