### UnusedMethodCollector Implementation

Source: https://github.com/phpstan/phpstan-src/blob/2.2.x/_autodocs/03-rules.md

Implements the Collector interface to identify and collect private methods within a class. It listens for `ClassMethod` nodes and returns an array containing details of private methods, including their class, name, file, and line number. This collector is intended to be processed by a `CollectedDataNode` rule.

```php
use PHPStan\Collectors\Collector;
use PHPStan\Collectors\CollectedData;
use PHPStan\Analyser\Scope;
use PhpParser\Node;
use PhpParser\Node\Stmt\ClassMethod;

final class UnusedMethodCollector implements Collector {
    public function getNodeType(): string {
        return ClassMethod::class;
    }

    public function processNode(Node $node, Scope $scope): CollectorData {
        // Collect all private methods
        if (!$node->isPrivate()) {
            return [];
        }

        $class = $scope->getClassReflection();
        if ($class === null) {
            return [];
        }

        return [
            'unused_methods' => [
                [
                    'class' => $class->getName(),
                    'method' => $node->name->toString(),
                    'file' => $scope->getFile(),
                    'line' => $node->getStartLine(),
                ]
            ]
        ];
    }
}
```

